<Base title="Appearing in the District of New Jersey — Federal Bench Reference">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;›&nbsp; Appearing in D.N.J.</div>
  <div class="judgehead">
    <h1>Appearing from outside New Jersey</h1>
    <div class="role">Admission, association, and how cases are assigned</div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Pro hac vice</h2>
    <p class="summary">Counsel admitted elsewhere may appear in this district pro hac vice under
    L. Civ. R. 101.1(c). The rule requires association with a member of the bar of this court who
    signs the pleadings and remains responsible in the matter.</p>
    <p class="summary">This page states the rule and argues nothing. Read the rule and the judge's
    own standing orders before relying on either.</p>
    <div class="footlinks">
      <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/court-info/local-rules-and-orders" rel="noopener">Local rules and orders</a>
      <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/standing-orders" rel="noopener">Standing orders</a>
      <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/judicial-preferences" rel="noopener">Judicial preferences</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Vicinages</h2>
    <p class="summary">The district sits in Camden, Newark and Trenton. Case assignment follows the
    court's published vicinage lines rather than the convenience of counsel.</p>
    <div class="footlinks">
      <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/vicinage-lines-case-assignment" rel="noopener">Vicinage lines and case assignment</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
